Database migrations (Alembic, through Flask-Migrate).

The app applies these automatically when it starts, after writing a backup copy of
the database to <instance>/backups/. See app/dbmaint.py.

When you change app/models.py:
  1. flask --app wsgi db migrate --rev-id 0002_short_name -m "what changed"
  2. Read the new file in migrations/versions/ and correct it if needed
     (Alembic cannot detect renamed columns, for example).
  3. Run the tests: tests/test_migrations.py fails if models and migrations differ.
  4. Commit the new file together with the model change.

Never edit a migration that has already been released; add a new one.
